# the current locale. Otherwise, it returns c." (tolower likewise), so EOF
# comes back as EOF and every byte but the 26 letters comes back as it is,
# 0xe0..0xfe included (the "C" locale has no letter there). A result that is
# a byte is printed as that byte, in diff_output.sh's notation.

